{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-six-unusual-traditions-from-six-more-places/audio/main-c0fd7b9d0114.mp3","durationSec":259.008,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.94,"text":"The Night of the Radishes takes place every December 23 in Oaxaca, Mexico."},{"start":5.74,"end":9.4,"text":"A radish is a vegetable, but here it becomes material for art."},{"start":10.16,"end":14.1,"text":"People carve oversized radishes into scenes and compete for prizes."},{"start":15.06,"end":20.58,"text":"The tradition began with farmers who wanted to attract customers at the Christmas market in the main square."},{"start":21.42,"end":24.8,"text":"Their carved vegetables helped people notice what they were selling."},{"start":25.68,"end":28.74,"text":"The city started the formal competition in 1897."},{"start":29.66,"end":34.86,"text":"Timing matters because radishes wilt, or lose their fresh shape, soon after cutting."},{"start":35.92,"end":40.74,"text":"The works are shown for only a few hours, and visitors wait in very long lines."},{"start":41.46,"end":44.78,"text":"There are also works made from corn husks and dried flowers."},{"start":45.96,"end":53.22,"text":"The Olney Pancake Race happens in Olney, Buckinghamshire, England, on Pancake Day, also called Shrove Tuesday."},{"start":54.02,"end":56.18,"text":"The traditional runners are women."},{"start":56.76,"end":60.3,"text":"They wear a scarf and an apron and carry a frying pan along a course."},{"start":60.84,"end":63.26,"text":"They must toss their pancake at the start and the finish."},{"start":64.22,"end":67.36,"text":"The story behind the tradition goes back to 1445."},{"start":68.18,"end":71.46,"text":"A woman was busy making pancakes when she heard the church bells."},{"start":72.22,"end":74.88,"text":"She ran to church still carrying her pan and pancake."},{"start":75.7,"end":77.8,"text":"The race remembers that story through action."},{"start":78.38,"end":85.02,"text":"Since 1950, Olney and Liberal, Kansas, have held an International Pancake Day race and compared their times."},{"start":85.84,"end":89.84,"text":"A local tradition therefore also creates a connection between two places."},{"start":90.7,"end":96.52,"text":"In Gävle, Sweden, a giant goat made of straw stands at Castle Square in the centre of the city."},{"start":97.3,"end":100.84,"text":"It is a Yule goat, a goat figure connected with the Christmas season."},{"start":101.54,"end":106.56,"text":"Local community groups build it over two days at the beginning of Advent, the period leading up to Christmas."},{"start":106.8,"end":109.14,"text":"The first Gävle Goat appeared in 1966."},{"start":110.28,"end":118.44,"text":"Since 1986, there have been two goats: one built by the Southern Merchants and another by the Natural Science Club of the School of Vasa."},{"start":119.1,"end":122.94,"text":"Here, the main activity is building and displaying a seasonal figure."},{"start":123.74,"end":128.94,"text":"A new giant straw goat is put up every year at Castle Square in central Gävle."},{"start":128.94,"end":133.72,"text":"The Guérewol is a yearly courtship competition among the Wodaabe Fula people of Niger."},{"start":134.7,"end":137.8,"text":"Courtship means trying to attract someone as a possible partner."},{"start":138.64,"end":141.72,"text":"Young men wear rich decorations and traditional face painting."},{"start":141.72,"end":146.44,"text":"They stand in lines, dance, and sing to win the attention of young women."},{"start":147.1,"end":149.68,"text":"The dance is called the Yaake."},{"start":149.68,"end":155.74,"text":"The gathering happens when Wodaabe cattle herders meet at the southern edge of the Sahara before moving south for the dry season."},{"start":156.22,"end":159.22,"text":"These herders traditionally move from place to place with their animals."},{"start":159.96,"end":164.84,"text":"A main meeting place is In-Gall in northwest Niger, where there is a festival and a market."},{"start":165.5,"end":169.76,"text":"The Guérewol lasts about a week, bringing courtship and a seasonal gathering together."},{"start":170.5,"end":175.32,"text":"The Monkey Buffet Festival happens every year in Lopburi, Thailand, north of Bangkok."},{"start":175.94,"end":178.66,"text":"A buffet usually offers a range of food to choose from."},{"start":179.48,"end":183.24,"text":"Here, the food is for local crab-eating macaques, a kind of monkey."},{"start":183.94,"end":188.52,"text":"People give them fruit and vegetables, for example at the Phra Prang Sam Yod temple."},{"start":189.26,"end":191.62,"text":"Sometimes fruit is frozen inside blocks of ice."},{"start":192.34,"end":197.4,"text":"The activity centres on feeding the local monkeys, but sharing a town with them is not always simple."},{"start":197.82,"end":201.54,"text":"By 2024, Lopburi had about 3,000 monkeys."},{"start":202.26,"end":206.26,"text":"They caused problems for residents by taking bags, drinks, and food."},{"start":206.68,"end":210.88,"text":"The government started a campaign to catch monkeys and stop them from having babies."},{"start":210.88,"end":217.88,"text":"Beqa is an island in Fiji, about 10 kilometres south of the main island, Viti Levu."},{"start":217.88,"end":221.8,"text":"Several of Beqa’s nine villages are known for fire-walking."},{"start":221.8,"end":224.92,"text":"In this practice, people walk across hot stones."},{"start":225.32,"end":231.08,"text":"In Fiji, it is practised by the Sawau clan, a community group on Beqa."},{"start":231.08,"end":234.38,"text":"The approved accounts do not give one yearly date for this tradition."},{"start":235.18,"end":241.98,"text":"They do show its long history as something visitors came to see: it was already a tourist attraction in 1902."},{"start":241.98,"end":248.7,"text":"Fire-walking has different purposes around the world, including healing, faith, and entering adult life."},{"start":249.56,"end":253.72,"text":"Those general purposes do not establish one specific reason for Beqa’s practice."},{"start":254.64,"end":258.4,"text":"Here, we can identify a local tradition that also attracts visitors."}],"words":[{"text":"The","start":0,"end":0.12},{"text":"Night","start":0.12,"end":0.32},{"text":"of","start":0.32,"end":0.46},{"text":"the","start":0.46,"end":0.6},{"text":"Radishes","start":0.6,"end":0.96},{"text":"takes","start":0.96,"end":1.62},{"text":"place","start":1.62,"end":2},{"text":"every","start":2,"end":2.44},{"text":"December","start":2.44,"end":2.8},{"text":"23","start":2.8,"end":3.7},{"text":"in","start":3.7,"end":3.86},{"text":"Oaxaca","start":3.86,"end":4.4},{"text":"Mexico","start":4.6,"end":4.94},{"text":"A","start":5.74,"end":5.88},{"text":"radish","start":5.88,"end":6.28},{"text":"is","start":6.28,"end":6.52},{"text":"a","start":6.52,"end":6.64},{"text":"vegetable","start":6.64,"end":7.08},{"text":"but","start":7.48,"end":7.68},{"text":"here","start":7.68,"end":7.9},{"text":"it","start":7.9,"end":8.02},{"text":"becomes","start":8.02,"end":8.3},{"text":"material","start":8.3,"end":8.8},{"text":"for","start":8.8,"end":9.08},{"text":"art","start":9.08,"end":9.4},{"text":"People","start":10.16,"end":10.4},{"text":"carve","start":10.4,"end":10.86},{"text":"oversized","start":10.86,"end":11.46},{"text":"radishes","start":11.46,"end":12},{"text":"into","start":12,"end":12.3},{"text":"scenes","start":12.3,"end":12.82},{"text":"and","start":12.82,"end":13.2},{"text":"compete","start":13.2,"end":13.52},{"text":"for","start":13.52,"end":13.76},{"text":"prizes","start":13.76,"end":14.1},{"text":"The","start":15.06,"end":15.22},{"text":"tradition","start":15.22,"end":15.54},{"text":"began","start":15.54,"end":15.98},{"text":"with","start":15.98,"end":16.2},{"text":"farmers","start":16.2,"end":16.66},{"text":"who","start":16.66,"end":17.08},{"text":"wanted","start":17.08,"end":17.32},{"text":"to","start":17.32,"end":17.52},{"text":"attract","start":17.52,"end":17.86},{"text":"customers","start":17.86,"